{"generated":"2026-09-08","fields":["name","x","y","cluster","url","contest"],"coarse":[{"n":"Generative vision & robust training","d":"Pixel-level generation and restoration, detecting generated images, and the problems where the training recipe itself is the challenge: noise, shift, forgetting, adversaries."},{"n":"Model internals, physical systems & control","d":"Problems where you look inside a network or a physical process instead of fitting a black box: pruning and weight forensics, from-scratch algorithms, parameter recovery from dynamics, and agents acting on a grid."},{"n":"Retrieval, matching & concept editing","d":"Deciding which items belong together when the labels are gone, matching across modalities through frozen vision-language models, and intervening inside frozen generators."},{"n":"Anomaly detection, audio & forensic signals","d":"One-class and fault detection, spectrogram-domain audio, and classification problems whose label lives in an artefact of how the data was produced rather than in its content."},{"n":"Visual perception: detect, count, segment","d":"Recognition-side computer vision: where things are, how many there are, which pixels belong to what, including non-RGB imagery."},{"n":"Language: text, sequences & translation","d":"Natural-language processing: judging and classifying text, repairing damaged language models at the token level, and moving meaning between languages."},{"n":"LLM reasoning, word games & strategy","d":"Using a language model's knowledge under a game-like protocol, and writing policies that play stochastic games."},{"n":"Tabular & structured data","d":"Supervised learning on tables, ranking and recommendation, and problems where the object of study is itself a model or a dataset."}],"fine":[{"n":"Image reconstruction & generated-image detection","c":0,"d":"Concept domain: inverse problems in pixel space and generative fingerprints. Quantise, inpaint, colourise, compress or reconstruct an image from very little, build autoencoders, and detect diffusion- or GAN-generated pictures by the artefacts the generator leaves behind."},{"n":"Training recipes: noise, shift, forgetting, distillation","c":0,"d":"Concept domain: the training procedure is the problem, not the architecture. Label noise and coreset selection, class imbalance, domain shift across scanners and visual styles, catastrophic forgetting and class-incremental learning, unlearning, dataset condensation, self-supervised pretraining, and reading a model's training data back off its weights."},{"n":"Adversarial attack & defence","c":0,"d":"Concept domain: adversarial examples. Craft perturbations that fool a frozen classifier, or write the loss that makes a model robust to them; includes attacks that must fool two targets at once."},{"n":"From-scratch algorithms & geometric fitting","c":1,"d":"Concept domain: classical machine-learning fundamentals implemented by hand. Lloyd's k-means and a linear SVM written from scratch, plus problems solved by fitting geometry directly: cluster a point cloud back into a picture, separate overlapping cards, choose continuous parameters that minimise a physical objective."},{"n":"White-box networks, pruning & hidden structure","c":1,"d":"Concept domain: the network as an object to inspect and edit. Prune it, deduce what a frozen weight-tied net computes, find which weights carry a hidden payload, fit a coordinate network to a shape, recover a hidden pattern set, decode a motor signal from neural recordings."},{"n":"Physical systems & parameter recovery","c":1,"d":"Concept domain: recover the mechanism or parameters behind observations. Identify an ordinary differential equation with a gap in the data, fit reaction kinetics, infer an orbital hierarchy from positions, predict molecular properties from geometry. One retrieval-over-tables question-answering task sits here by proximity."},{"n":"Grid-world control & imitation","c":1,"d":"Concept domain: sequential decision making on a grid. Behaviour cloning from demonstrations, next-action prediction, temporal-difference and Q-learning update rules, planning with a narrow field of view."},{"n":"Identity, alignment & recovering lost pairings","c":2,"d":"Concept domain: work out which items belong together after the correspondence was destroyed. Same-author attribution and clustering, matching audio to video, aligning two embedding spaces, un-shuffling rows, ordering the turns of a conversation."},{"n":"Cross-modal retrieval with frozen CLIP","c":2,"d":"Concept domain: match images to text or to each other through a frozen vision-language model. Identity retrieval and re-identification, captions scored by a text metric, prompt-side attacks, style-invariant odd-one-out, projecting a new language into CLIP's text space."},{"n":"Editing concepts inside frozen generators","c":2,"d":"Concept domain: intervene in a frozen diffusion model or language model so it swaps one concept for another, or edit a photo so a classifier reads a different class while the picture still looks unchanged."},{"n":"Anomaly detection & fault localisation","c":3,"d":"Concept domain: train on normal data only, then flag or localise the abnormal. Industrial defect heat maps, ECG windows, seismic fault intervals, reactor instability, patch-level scoring in a latent space."},{"n":"Audio classification & forensics","c":3,"d":"Concept domain: spectrogram-domain audio. Vocal effort, environmental and event classification, tempo manipulation and synthetic-speech detection, blind source separation, and a pitch-perception puzzle."},{"n":"Forensic classification from encoded or leaky data","c":3,"d":"Concept domain: the label sits in an artefact of how the data was made rather than in its content. Metadata and file properties, a known corruption pipeline, deliberately encoded features, behavioural traces, extrapolating a scaling law, extending a deployed classifier head. The least homogeneous cluster in the map: these problems share a forensic stance rather than a data type."},{"n":"Detection, counting & scene structure","c":4,"d":"Concept domain: find and count things in a picture. Axis-aligned and oriented bounding boxes, density-map counting, weakly supervised detection, tile and collage structure, scene-graph triplets, counting questions about images."},{"n":"Localisation & saliency from frozen vision models","c":4,"d":"Concept domain: point at the right region with little or no supervision. Saliency maps, dense text-aligned readout from a frozen CLIP, text-conditioned boxes, one-shot foreground masks, fine-grained individual re-identification, reading text from single-character supervision."},{"n":"Dense segmentation & multi-channel imaging","c":4,"d":"Concept domain: per-pixel prediction and inputs that are not ordinary photographs. U-Net segmentation, radar and multispectral channels, satellite rain masks, medical scans and histopathology, multi-label presence vectors, and regression of coordinates out of an image."},{"n":"Token-level repair, segmentation & decipherment","c":5,"d":"Concept domain: work at the character and token level. Repair a sabotaged embedding table or a scrambled tokenizer, segment text that has no delimiters, correct errors position by position, break a substitution cipher, untangle two interleaved paragraphs."},{"n":"Text classification, verification & AI-text forensics","c":5,"d":"Concept domain: judge a piece of text. Topic and toxicity classification, claim verification against evidence, semantic equivalence, hallucination scoring, detecting or evading AI-text detectors, faithful rationales, span extraction, syntactic parsing."},{"n":"Translation & cross-lingual transfer","c":5,"d":"Concept domain: move meaning between languages or between programming languages. Implement attention sequence-to-sequence from empty stubs, invert a translation model, transfer labels from English to an unlabelled language, retrieve across languages, chain translations round-trip."},{"n":"Word games, QA & program semantics","c":6,"d":"Concept domain: use a language model's knowledge under a game-like protocol. Word-association and riddle games, interactive twenty-questions with a judge, multiple-choice question answering, recovering the prompt from an answer, few-shot relational analogies, predicting what a program prints."},{"n":"Game-playing strategies under uncertainty","c":6,"d":"Concept domain: write a policy that plays a stochastic game where the metric is money or wins. Bluffing and calling in Liar's Dice, including with language-model agents, and a betting strategy at a casino table."},{"n":"Tabular learning & model-space introspection","c":7,"d":"Concept domain: supervised learning on tables, plus the problems where the thing being studied is a model or a dataset. Counterfactual inputs, feature engineering inside a fixed pipeline, contaminated training data, deciding which model produced these outputs, membership inference, choosing which rows and columns to keep."},{"n":"Ranking & recommendation","c":7,"d":"Concept domain: output an ordering or a set instead of a single label. Top-K recommendations, ranking contest participants, multi-label category assignment from collaborative-filtering embeddings."},{"n":"Plain tabular regression & classification","c":7,"d":"Concept domain: standard supervised prediction on tabular data, sometimes with a procedural twist such as submitting through a fixed pipeline or counting rows into bins, rather than a modelling insight."}],"tasks":[["Aarav's Project Prometheus",0.3551,0.3841,10,"https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/sota-aaravs-project-prometheus","SOTA - AI Community"],["About Cinderella (O popoluške)",0.3642,0.5161,12,"https://judge.nitro-ai.org/competitions/slovenska-olympiada/slovak-aoi-2026/3/view","Slovakia 2026"],["Adversarial Attacks",0.0899,0.451,2,"https://github.com/OlimpiadaAI/I-OlimpiadaAI/tree/main/first_stage/adversarial_attacks","Poland 2024 Stage I"],["Adversarial Protection",0.0999,0.4136,